This code defines a Virus class and a Person class. The Virus class has methods to infect and kill people. The Person class has methods to post, like, comment, and share on a social media platform. The main function simulates an outbreak of the virus on the platform.
The virus can be spread through the comments and shares made by infected people. The transmission rate determines the probability that an uninfected person will become infected after being exposed to the virus. The mortality rate determines the probability that an infected person will die.
The symptoms of the virus are represented by the virus's name. In this example, the symptoms are fever. People who have the symptoms are more likely to die or recover, and they are also more likely to be exposed to the virus.
The age of a person affects the person's chance of dying from the virus. Older people are more susceptible to the virus. The virus's mortality rate is higher for older people.
The virus's transmission rate is lower for people who have recently been infected.
